      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you please write a unit test for this to assert that we have ported the correct business logic from multi-tree?\n\ne.g. \n```\ncc_binary {\n  name: \"vendor_bin\",\n  shared_libs: [\"liblog\"],\n  vendor: true,\n}\n\ncc_binary {\n  name: \"vendor_bin_compiling_against_sdk\",\n  shared_libs: [\"liblog\"],\n  sdk_version: \"current\",\n  vendor: true,\n}\n\n```\nMy understanding was that the latter should compile against the ndk variant of liblog, but IIUC, this implementation does not respect `sdk_version` and links the latter against the llndk/vendorapi variant of liblog",
